  "raw": " London on May 22 and spent 14 days receiving treatments before returning home on Friday.\n\nLast week, he led several top local government leaders in Jigawa state on his daily walks to the state house in Dutse for official functions — unusual behaviour by a man who spent most of his life untrained at speaking Kaduna Hausa.\n\n“Since he came back from London, it looks like he can no longer control his anger that has been bothering him due to health challenges,'' his wife told Daily Trust, adding: “I just pray for him a speedy recovery.''\n\nAbyei she said was not in aised hands. She was still insisting on controlling its ownership as per certain rules established when British colonists occupied it under the 1945 Anglo-African Convention establishing multiparty elections between North of Africa (NAF) rebels and northern Ba’athist military regime?\n\nAn aide who is familiar with Mrs Aisha's closeness to the president told",
  "serialized": "London on May 22 and spent 14 days receiving treatments before returning home on Friday. Last week, he led several top local government leaders in Jigawa state on his daily walks to the state house in Dutse for official functions — unusual behaviour by a man who spent most of his life untrained at speaking Kaduna Hausa. “Since he came back from London, it looks like he can no longer control his anger that has been bothering him due to health challenges,'' his wife told Daily Trust, adding: “I just pray for him a speedy recovery.'' Abyei she said was not in aised hands. She was still insisting on controlling its ownership as per certain rules established when British colonists occupied it under the 1945 Anglo-African Convention establishing multiparty elections between North of Africa (NAF) rebels and northern Ba’athist military regime? An aide who is familiar with Mrs Aisha's closeness to the president told",
